              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">cfe7050c-dcd1-496d-bb68-08dfd0624c66</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Reusable helper definitions, shared by several buttons.

CAMERA SETTINGS define how the user can navigate once a camera is active: field of view, pan / rotation / zoom on or off, auto adjust, auto rotation speed, position restriction, zoom distance and polar / azimuth rotation limits.
- TopSettings: rotation disabled, so the top view stays a plan view.
Note: in the current viewer, cameras with settings are switched to instantly, so settings are best used with assign actions (button 1), not with moves or animations.

CAMERA MOTION defines how the camera travels to its new state: duration (seconds), easing and interpolation (used for paths through several cameras).
- SmoothMotion: 2 s, Cubic.InOut.
- OrbitMotion: 8 s, Linear.None for a constant speed, CatmullRom interpolation (the default value, so it doesn't appear in the JSON).</item>
                  </items>
