                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">a488a9f6-b2a9-4409-83c6-86c225a3a92e</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Button 1 - Assign a preset camera.

The Camera input of the Camera component receives the name of a predefined camera: Perspective, Top, Bottom, Left, Right, Front or Back (also available in the right-click menu &gt; ShapeDiver Helpers).

With a camera name and no position / target, the Camera Action creates an "assign" action: the viewer switches to this camera. The Camera Settings travel with the camera (here: no rotation).
Assign actions don't use a Camera Motion.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
