                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Button 2 - Move the camera to a custom position and target.

The Camera component receives a Type (Perspective), a Position and a Target. With a single camera, the Camera Action creates a "set" action: the viewer switches back to the perspective camera (e.g. after the top view) and moves it to the new position with the Camera Motion (SmoothMotion: 2 s, Cubic.InOut).

No Camera Settings are given here: with settings, the move would not be animated in the current viewer.</item>
