                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Button 3 - Animate the camera along a path.

13 points on a circle (radius 20 m, 8 m above the ground; the first point is repeated at the end to close the loop) are used as camera positions, all looking at the box centre.

When the Camera Action receives several cameras, it creates an "animate" action that moves through all of them with the Camera Motion.

The Type of an animation is taken from the FIRST camera only. We therefore split the first point off, make it a Perspective camera, and merge it back in front of the other cameras.</item>
                  </items>
